  "method": "Actual installed Common session runtime and Squish codec, one player. One-second warmup followed by four measured seconds per scene; synthetic clock advances at the declared tick rate. Each realm uses its authored board with the most frosted cells. Zen and Rush use the same seed with their normal empty goals/frost. Active scenes make ordinary engine-selected legal swaps and finish their real cascades; content selection and unlocked progress are diagnostic fixtures, not a user playthrough. Swaps are prepared before timing, which measures tick, scene generation, serialization, one player buffer and byte comparison. Payload counts only byte-distinct frames, modeling duplicate suppression for one remote self-hosted player. Browser-local solo play has no remote frame upload. Excludes transport overhead, loading, browser rendering, mobile hardware and WAN. Asset bytes are raw media excluding encoding/protocol overhead. Frame and pool bounds are asserted; existing Scene tests cover constructed peak effects separately.",
